Deployment Workflows
We chose controlled deployments over the auto deploy feature render offers due to how we ship features to our various environments and also tagging every deployment.
Our approach:
Auto-deploy is DISABLED for both STAG and PROD services
New GitHub Actions workflows with a flow similar to what we are familiar with:
Tag-based deployments for version control
Manual triggers for control
Automatic secrets injection (no manual dashboard updates)
Health checks after deployment
Automatic tagging on successful STAG deployment
Checking for tag existence and deployment from a particular tag for PROD deployment
 All Render deployment workflows are prefixed with RENDER- for easy identification. eg, RENDER-botai-deploy-stag.yml, RENDER-be-app-deploy-prod.yml, etc.
Monitoring Workflows: ping-be-app-render.yml - Keep services warm (STAG + PROD)

Notifications and Monitoring
We evaluated two options for service notifications and chose email based on cost considerations.
Option 1: Webhooks → Google Chat
Cost: $19/month for Professional workspace upgrade.
Additional cost: Hosting a webhook receiver service and keeping alive without spin-downs
Benefit: Real-time chat notifications
Verdict: Too expensive for our current scale and user volume. This beats the purpose of the double setup of the hobby workspaces to cut cost as discussed at the beginning of the document
Option 2: Email Notifications (CHOSEN)
Cost: Free
Coverage: Deployment failures, service downtime, build failures
Delivery: Email to configured recipients
Verdict: Sufficient for our current needs, although we would need to be constantly checking our emails
Render Email Notifications Configuration (using option 2)
Current Setup: The notification set to "All notifications" on both workspace PROD and STAG for all services
